2.1.1 The members of the Association shall be
divided into the following categories:
(a) Land surveyor members;
(b) Life members;
(c) Honorary members;
(d) Surveyors - in - training members;
(e) Associate members;
(f) Retired members; and
(g) Student members.
Added January 2019

2.5.1 The following categories of members can use
the “NBLS” designation after their name:
(a) Land surveyor members;
(b) Life members;
(c) Associate members provided they were once a
land surveyor member;
(d) Honorary members provided they were once a
land surveyor member; and
(e) Retired members.
Revised January 2019

5.1.3 The Executive Council shall be elected by the
vote of the members who have the right to vote in
their respective zone and shall hold office for three
years. The election of councillors shall be as follows:
(a) Year 1:
one councillor in the Moncton zone;
one councillor in the Fredericton zone;
(b) Year 2:
one councillor in the North West zone;
one councillor in the provincial zone;
one councillor in the Saint John zone;
(c) Year 3:
one councillor in the North East zone;
one councillor in the provincial zone.
Revised January 2005

